  "body": "Hello lovely humans,\n\n[preact](https://www.npmjs.com/package/preact) just published its new version 6.2.0.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      State\n    </th>\n    <td>\n      Update :rocket:\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Dependency\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      preact\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      New version\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      6.2.0\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Type\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      devDependency\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nThis version is **not covered** by your **current version range**.\n\nWithout accepting this pull request your project will work just like it did before. There might be a bunch of new features, fixes and perf improvements that the maintainers worked on for you though.\n\nI recommend you look into these changes and try to get onto the latest version of preact.\nGiven that you have a decent test suite, a passing build is a strong indicator that you can take advantage of these changes by merging the proposed change into your project. Otherwise this branch is a great starting point for you to work on the update.\n\nDo you have any ideas how I could improve these pull requests? Did I report anything you think isn’t right?\nAre you unsure about how things are supposed to work?\n\nThere is a collection of [frequently asked questions](https://greenkeeper.io/faq.html) and while I’m just a bot, there is a group of people who are happy to teach me new things. [Let them know](https://github.com/greenkeeperio/greenkeeper/issues/new).\n\nGood luck with your project :sparkles:\n\nYou rock!\n\n:palm_tree:\n\n---\n\nThe new version differs by 24 commits .\n- [`5f3189e`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/5f3189ec56608e9779ac1359b212d560c32eed3d) <code>6.2.0</code>\n- [`6bfa2af`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/6bfa2af9f5d2fb48c3e3b075b3f5e6dc85c4749c) <code>Drop a few bytes off the render queue.</code>\n- [`1475824`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/14758246ff8c97232ba648d9d154e4bad080c053) <code>Fix: Re-add `Component.prototype.render` since libraries like `preact-compat` use that to determine if a function is a pure functional component or a classful component. Instead of returning `null`, it is now empty.</code>\n- [`11ac72a`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/11ac72a6abc0fc7c86da9a0ed98e90a212efeef5) <code>Inline remaining `empty()` calls.</code>\n- [`9467e2a`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/9467e2ab893b7b3a487fa23e0dec490cceb7914c) <code>Consolidate prop cache check + populate into the diff entry.</code>\n- [`c289ce6`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/c289ce62c2f808951814ad60db53bc8aca6dbf2b) <code>Switch to lazy empty check</code>\n- [`cc03a7a`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/cc03a7a579c9dffcd599ad075b6562a6ff0b34e9) <code>Add performance test for JSX VNode creation.</code>\n- [`49893be`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/49893beb162f9bad16a71b85c07d756ba8644e2c) <code>Tests: if `NODE_ENV=production`, run performance tests against `preact.min.js`.</code>\n- [`e973347`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/e973347b54fda46ed5d601d6e5b87f52f814b896) <code>Remove tests for `getInitialState()`, which is no longer unofficially supported in Preact core (it is still supported in `preact-compat`).</code>\n- [`e083f35`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/e083f3583c2f0a632a45c2d4c538e4ac036b07ef) <code>Add tests for nested children 👯</code>\n- [`f389dd3`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/f389dd376c8fc90e92eb643583afbc0a49dc8930) <code>Remove unnecessary early exit for a condition that rarely/never occurs.</code>\n- [`b1e1704`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/b1e17045ec6d1fbf41c17c58ed6d22149616a6e3) <code>Fix sort-of regression in `6.1.0` whether state changes in `componentDidUpdate()` resulted in synchronous re-renders.</code>\n- [`ee4f61c`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/ee4f61c8f4ffb017b4afaca44b59472b268f4b41) <code>`._disableRendering` --> `._disable` to save a few bytes</code>\n- [`2e75116`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/2e751162a2cb51ff5b45309e60468e89215612dd) <code>Remove unnecessary uses of `empty()`</code>\n- [`45c12ef`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/45c12efdb5a047e73288bc07fe9aae1399617e63) <code>Potentially breaking change: remove undocumented support for `getInitialState()` on classful components. This has never been part of the API but was left in core in order to support `preact-compat`'s use. It is now being moved into `preact-compat`. This allows preact to normalize class components that don't inherit from Component.</code>\n\nThere are 24 commits in total. See the [full diff](https://github.com/developit/preact/compare/7ade27579ffce259fa34be58ef48e6bbdd1919b4...5f3189ec56608e9779ac1359b212d560c32eed3d).\n\n---\n\nThis pull request was created by [greenkeeper.io](https://greenkeeper.io/).\n\n<sub>Tired of seeing this sponsor message? :zap: `greenkeeper upgrade`</sub>\n",
